{"id":"sh/n2dk3etc","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":287,"top":235,"width":945,"height":36},"text":"Barnard’s Star: Recognize apparent motion","style":{"fontSize":26,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#D7FC70","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/m143u9cr","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":287,"top":278,"width":945,"height":94},"text":"At similar wavelengths near 2.0 µm, the glow shifts north while neighboring stars remain nearly fixed. The learner can support a qualitative motion interpretation and explain why saturation limits a precise measurement.","style":{"fontSize":22.51,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
